From db2ebd07d450f25c89e734a17c97debb3c0fbb02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 12:22:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Occupancy curve: count intervals intersecting each period
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace point-in-time sampling (start ≤ t ≤ end at N daily points)
with period-intersection counting (start < period_end AND end ≥ period_start).

Each bar now answers "how many records overlap this year/month/day?"
rather than "what is the peak simultaneous count at any instant in this period?".

Changes:
- compute_occupancy_curve: period-based bucket join replacing daily time axis
- compute_column_occupancy (occupancy mode): same, removes the max re-aggregation step
- _store_raw_temporal: cache raw interval endpoints instead of point-in-time counts
- recompute_temporal_charts: count period intersections from cached interval data

https://claude.ai/code/session_01FcM13EbRQGRFswRkWxecy2
